# Which std/aata constructs should become DEFINITION BLOCKS

Survey after `definition` landed (2026-09-24). The test is the one settled during
the design: **a DEFINITION introduces a symbol by giving its meaning in terms of
others; a THEORY AXIOM constrains a primitive that has no meaning beyond its
axioms.** Syntax cannot tell these apart — both are `func f(…) => U` plus an
equation — so every candidate below is judged on that question.

---

## TIER 1 — clear definitions, should migrate

Each builds its symbol out of ALREADY-MEANINGFUL parts. Nothing is being
assumed; the equation IS the symbol's meaning.

### Recursive definitions (multi-clause — the form definition blocks exist for)

| file | symbol | clauses |
|---|---|---|
| `std/peano.bpa` | `add` | `addZeroLeft` + `addSuccLeft` |
| `std/peano.bpa` | `mul` | `mulZeroLeft` + `mulSuccLeft` |
| `std/peano/subtraction.bpa` | `sub` | `subZeroRight` + `subSuccSucc` + `subZeroLeft` |
| `std/integer.bpa` | `add` | `addZeroLeft` + `addSuccLeft` + `addPrevLeft` |
| `std/integer.bpa` | `neg` | `negZero` + `negSucc` + `negPrev` |
| `std/integer.bpa` | `mul` | `mulZeroLeft` + `mulSuccLeft` + `mulPrevLeft` |
| `std/integer/divides.bpa` | `pow` | `powZero` + `powSucc` |
| `std/group/power.bpa` | `power` | `powerZero` + `powerSucc` + `powerPrev` |
| `std/sequence.bpa` | `foldUpTo` | `foldZero` + `foldSucc` |
| `std/group/sequence.bpa` | `productUpTo` | `productUpToZero` + `productUpToSucc` |
| `std/group/sequence.bpa` | `revProductUpTo` | `revProductZero` + `revProductSucc` |
| `std/integer/product.bpa` | `productUpTo` | `productUpToZero` + `productUpToSucc` |
| `std/integer/sum.bpa` | `sumUpTo` | `sumUpToZero` + `sumUpToSucc` |

**These are the flagship cases.** `add(ZERO,b) = b; add(succ(a),b) = succ(add(a,b))`
is *the* definition of addition, and today it is two separately-named axioms that
a reader must notice belong together. A definition block says so.

### Single-clause definitions

| file | symbol | axiom |
|---|---|---|
| `std/integer.bpa` | `sub` | `definitionOfSubtraction` — `sub(a,b) = add(a, neg(b))` |
| `std/rational.bpa` | `sub` / `succ` / `prev` | `subDefinition` / `succDefinition` / `prevDefinition` |
| `std/real.bpa` | `sub` / `succ` / `prev` | same three |
| `std/complex.bpa` | `conj` | `conjDef` |
| `std/integer/mod-n.bpa` | `znPower` | `znPowerDef` |

The names already say it (`…Definition`, `…Def`).

### Predicate definitions (the `iff` sites)

| file | symbol | axiom |
|---|---|---|
| `std/function.bpa` | `invertible` | `invertibleDef` |
| `std/integer/mod-n.bpa` | `isUnit` | `isUnitCharacterization` |

Both introduce the predicate and nothing else constrains it.

